{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1497332862,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyMzU0NDIzNjk=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1570","origin":"github"},"title":"URL candidate generation broken on windows","message":"As it can be seen in the following screenshot, the URL candidate for a subdataset has the form: `URL/some\\.git` on windows, while it should be `URL/some/.git`. This could either be broken code for the generation of URL candidates in `get`, or a relative URL that is read from .gitmodules and needs mangling. I somewhat suspect the use of `normpath/join` in `_get_flexible_source_candidates()` to be the culprit. If that is the case, we should use `normpath/join` from the `posixpath` modules, instead of the platform default `os.path`, for non-path RIs.\n\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/136479/27048481-4fc190c4-4fac-11e7-9dbb-81fad60f4cc1.png)","files":null}]}